From 450698e796f037e4b6a1207435e237800a90ec5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: banyanleaf <banyanleaf@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:35:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stop advertising kitty graphics herdr cannot deliver

Pane terminals answered a child's Kitty graphics capability query from their
own parser state, which never reflected what Herdr could render. A probing
TUI therefore chose Kitty over Sixel (or over its text fallback), painted a
raster, and nothing appeared - while the fallback it had been showing was
already replaced. On terminals without the protocol the text art vanished
too, so the only symptom was a brief flash and no error.

Two gaps caused that:

- terminal.kitty_graphics = false only skipped enabling the protocol, so the
  pane terminal kept libghostty's default image quota and still answered a=q
  with OK. A zero quota disables the protocol outright, which is what the
  setting promises.
- The outer terminal's own capability was never consulted. The client now
  probes it before the handshake (the a=q plus DA1 sentinel query that
  image-capable TUIs send), reports the answer as an optional endpoint hello
  field, and the server gates pane graphics on the setting and on an attached
  client that can render. Live pane terminals are re-applied when that answer
  changes; a client that never reports it, and a session with no client
  attached, keep the previous optimistic answer.

Verified on Windows Terminal from WSL: a pane child now receives only DA1 and
falls back to its text art, while Kitty, Ghostty and WezTerm keep answering
OK. Windows clients keep the optimistic answer; they have no host probe yet.
